  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road Autumn 2005 was held in Osaka on 23 October, Tokyo on 30 October and Nagoya on 3 November 2005. Its official tournament, the Battle Road Stadium, was a new six-stage format: players battled each other through five stages, then a researcher of the Pokémon Card Laboratory (PCL) in the last, and a loss sent them back to the first stage. Everyone got Ryo Ueda's Pikachu δ, a win at the fourth stage earned three holo Holon Energies, and beating PCL earned the Stadium card Battle Road Stadium.",
